      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While scent marketing is a real tactic used in retail appealing to subconscious triggers, the idea of grocery stores pumping out aerosolized neuro-stimulants is highly speculative and currently not supported by mainstream consumer science. The strongest evidence points toward olfactory cues influencing emotional responses and memory recall, prompting desired purchases. If you find this pattern stressful, it might be worth exploring environmental factors or potential behavioral influences rather than assuming chemical manipulation.",
